the clark county school district laying  the groundwork to get some students and  staff back into the classroom  kate houston joins us live in the  newsroom with some more clarification  from the district on how it plans to  accomplish this next step kate  yes today's superintendent dr jesus  jarrah said while there is no  set timeline or deadline if planning  goes smoothly there could be groups back  on campus by late february or early  march  last night the board of trustees  approved an agreement to eventually move  kindergarten through third grade into  a hybrid model principals will also be  able to bring small groups of students  who need extra support onto separate  campuses and that would be entirely  voluntary  dr jarrah says data from ccea shows a  majority of teachers  want to be back in class with students  he feels confident there will be enough  teachers to help the kids  now parents are weighing in trying to  decide what's best for their children  it's not safe to put a timeline on it  right now  so this was them you know like oh yeah  we want to do all these things  but we don't know when with six kids i  have six different mentalities  six different needs i have you know from  extremely  extremely smart extremely extremely  chatty too  quiet i mean all kinds of of needs there  and i feel that they need to be in  school in order to get kids back in the  classroom  principals will need to submit their  plan to a regional superintendent for  approval  dr jara says they are working together  to ensure there is equity for students  across the entire district another  factor in this decision is the high  covet 19 positivity rate in the state  dr jarrah says he is working with the  county to hopefully start vaccinating  teachers  by the end of this month back to you all  right thanks kate now we did ask on  twitter do you understand ccsd's plan  toward reopening schools  84 percent of you who waited said nope  16 said yes well we understand this  process is confusing  and there are no clear-cut answers at  this point but we promise you  eight news now is constantly working to  find answers for all of you
 

